 I have  apologized for mistakes I made in how we  handled allegations of a cleric getting  involved in Muskaan  with an adult I have never ever  knowingly and intentionally left a  priest in ministry who I knew had abused  a child or moved him from one assignment  to another or let him stay in ministry  ever the Whitacre now joins us at the  table bill good morning good morning so  what do you make of that statement bill  well we do know that this year once the  allegations started to percolate in  Buffalo the bishop has taken some  actions but we also know from the  documents and from our reporting that  for years there were priests who had  credible accusations of sexual  harassment and in one case statutory  rape and little or nothing was done and  was only once this started to come to  light that the church in Buffalo started  to take some action well one of the  whistleblowers you talked to was the  bishops executive assistant you don't  get much closer to a person than their  executive assistant though who normally  knows everything about what's going on  what can you tell us about her and why  did she decide to speak up now she told  us that she felt compelled to speak  compelled by her faith and by her  religion to speak up she went into the  job it was her dream job she was working  for the bishop and she's a very very  faithful person and she started to see  things that just didn't seem right did  she say something to him about it she  did she was getting phone calls from  victims she was answering the phone and  she would just hear repeatedly of these  stories of people who had been abused by  priests and she tried to get the bishop  to address this and she also she always  felt as though she were getting the  brush-off you know not now not now and  this went on for a while and she felt  the only way she could handle this was  to start to leak this information that  she had you could sense the anger from  the deacon what finally motivated him to  call for the resignation of Bishop  Malone  first of all the information he didn't  know who the whistleblower was but this  information is being revealed on  television in Buffalo one of the priests  in the documents was the priest in his  parish and the documents and that  evidence about that priest just was it  was the last straw for him so he's  taking me within the Catholic Church the  extraordinary step of calling for the  bishop to resign it's been 16 years  since the church scandal in Boston the  cuts started all of this the movie  spotlight if everybody remembers that  what do you think makes this different  well in terms of what we've learned  about Buffalo what makes this one  different is that we've got this  whistleblower inside who is revealing  this information and the information  it's it's hundreds and hundreds of pages  of memos emails personnel files that  show that the church knew that these  activities were going on and took steps  not to address it but to in her words  cover it up Wow I'll be watching oh yeah  they're always incredible reporting I  know by you and the producers it's a few  minutes great job you can see Bill's  entire report on 60 minutes this Sunday  right here on CBS
 

